<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Unknown components of parallel vectors</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\mathbf{p} = \begin{pmatrix} x \\ \displaystyle{@m2@} \\ \displaystyle{@m3@} \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{q} = \begin{pmatrix} \displaystyle{@n1@} \\ y \\ \displaystyle{@n3@} \end{pmatrix}\) are parallel, with \(\mathbf{p} = k\mathbf{q}\). Fractions or decimals are fine.</p><div>(a) \(k =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) \(y =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Every component of \(\mathbf{p}\) is \(k\) times the matching component of \(\mathbf{q}\).</p><p>(a) The bottom components are both known: \({@m3@} = k \times ({@n3@})\), so \(k = {@kk@}\).</p><p>(b) \(x = k \times ({@n1@}) = {@xx@}\).</p><p>(c) \({@m2@} = k\,y\), so \(y = {@m2@} \div k = {@yy@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: unknown components of parallel vectors, k found first. xx, yy stand for the letters x, y shown in the stem. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Exercise C, Q6. */
plist: [[-5,5,1,2],[-1,3,-2,-2],[-4,-4,-1,3],[3,-6,2,-3],[-2,-4,-4,3/2],[-5,-6,-2,-3/2],[3,-6,-2,1/2],[-2,2,4,-1/2],[4,-4,1,4],[-3,-2,2,-5/2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
n1: plist[ix][1]; yy: plist[ix][2]; n3: plist[ix][3]; kk: plist[ix][4];
m2: kk*yy; m3: kk*n3; xx: kk*n1;
kinv: 1/kk; xinv: n1/kk; ymul: kk*m2;
k1: kk+1; xft: (kk+1)*n1; yft: m2/(kk+1);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, k={@kk@}, x={@xx@}, y={@yy@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: unknown components of parallel vectors</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Find the scalar k and two unknown components when two three-dimensional vectors are parallel.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 6 in Exercise C of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: the scalar found first as its own part, unknowns in both vectors, new numbers, randomised over a curated list, with named and follow-through feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
